<title>PARAGUAY: Paraguay budget plans bond issue to cover deficit.</title>
<headline>Paraguay budget plans bond issue to cover deficit.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paraguayan government plans to issue a $100 million bond early next year to help cover its spending needs in 1997, according to budget projections Tuesday.</p>
<p>The budget, currently under discussion in Congress, foresees a deficit of $360 million, which will have to be covered by bond issues in the capital markets and through loans from international organizations.</p>
<p>-- Jose Maria Amarilla, Asuncion Newsroom, 595 21 444527</p>
</text>
